      "columns": 2,
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The Galleria bag debuted in 2007, named after the brand's first boutique in Milan's Galleria Vittorio Emanuele II. Its silhouette borrows from 1940s frame bags and doctor bags, featuring a clean trapezoid shape with curved top handles. It earned the nickname \"killer bag\" after being used by assassin Sabine Moreau in the film Mission: Impossible—Ghost Protocol to conceal a gun.",
